{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>In you, YHWH, I have taken refuge</b> — it seems right to me that David composed this psalm, like the psalm \"Bless, my soul, YHWH, my Elohim; You are very great,\" for it is joined to it." "<b>In you</b> — You, HaShem, stand forever; therefore I shall never be ashamed."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 71, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:33:48.333466260Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}